From 3153a2603635c7e2c828fcd72c4ff300a98870fc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 08:14:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] tests: FakeHub/FakeService release share
 releaseDiagnostic + evidence helpers

Follow-up to PR #1960 exact-head review 5887860374 (three non-blocking
nits), checked against hermes-hub worker/src/transitions.ts
releaseTask/releaseDiagnostic on main:

- One helper for both routes: FakeService.release_diagnostic (as
  releaseDiagnostic) and FakeService.release_evidence (run metadata +
  event evidence) are used by the leases release (_release_run) and by
  FakeService.release_op, as the real releaseTask is one function for
  both. release_op now truncates past MAX_DIAGNOSTIC_CHARS, marks a
  protocol_violation crash in run metadata and merges a neutral
  release's extra (+ owner_restart) like the leases path. The
  protocol-violation streak stays unmodelled (docstring).
- Truncation length matches JSON.stringify(value).length: compact
  separators, ensure_ascii=False, counted in UTF-16 code units, so
  non-ASCII is not over-counted and astral characters count two.
- A diagnostic that is not an object (string, list, 0, false, "") is
  refused `invalid` for every outcome on both routes and changes
  nothing. As in releaseTask the check runs after fence() (a non-holder
  still gets lease_lost) and before any write.

Tests (tests/hermes_cli/test_kanban_sync_rejections.py): 82 new cases;
78 fail on the #1960 fake, the other 4 (leases-path ASCII truncation
and neutral extra) guard already-modelled behaviour. All 55 test files
importing kanban_sync_fake_board / FakeService: 1089 passed, 10 skipped.
